{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M3ToDWvK6qAGdQN8Nd4cHm","type":"tool_result","content":"Overview keys: ['structure', 'plot_summary', 'model_usage', 'timing']\n\nPlot summary:\n{'plot_summary': \"Montresor, the narrator of this chilling tale, begins by revealing his deep-seated grudge against Fortunato, a fellow nobleman in an unnamed Italian city during carnival season. Montresor meticulously plans to exact revenge on Fortunato without any risk or detection. He exploits the festive atmosphere and Fortunato's pride as a connoisseur of wine to lure him into the catacombs beneath the city under the pretense of verifying a pipe of Amontillado, an esteemed type of sherry.\\n\\nAs they descend deeper into the vaults, Montresor takes advantage of Fortunato's increasing intoxication and disorientation. The dark, labyrinthine catacombs filled with bones and dust serve as the perfect backdrop for Montresor to isolate his victim. He chains Fortunato inside a niche in the wall, beginning the gruesome task of sealing him within using masonry. Initially, Fortunato resists and pleads for mercy, but his strength wanes.\\n\\nThe climax occurs when Fortunato's resistance finally ceases, leaving Montresor to complete the masonry alone. The story concludes with a haunting reflection on how no one has disturbed the bones in the catacombs since that fateful night, hinting at the successful execution of Montresor's revenge and his subsequent escape from any consequences.\", 'themes': ['revenge', 'deception', 'guilt'], 'narrative_style': 'first-person retrospective'}\n\nThemes:\nNOT FOUND","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f700d47e-f086-4db4-997e-7b427eb3c6e7","uuid":"61953477-abf1-402c-b851-098af80d6e87","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Overview keys: ['structure', 'plot_summary', 'model_usage', 'timing']\n\nPlot summary:\n{'plot_summary': \"Montresor, the narrator of this chilling tale, begins by revealing his deep-seated g