{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JCEuriYr1yh8tb28i8xPWp","type":"tool_result","content":"    95→## Fix History\n    96→\n    97→### Attempt 1 (2026-01-18): Fixed validator heuristic\n    98→- Removed overly aggressive auto-acceptance of high-mention-count names\n    99→- Enhanced validation system prompt to reject objects/food/drink\n   100→- Result: Amontillado no longer extracted, narrator correctly identified in plot_summary\n   101→\n   102→### Attempt 2 (2026-01-18): Fixed NER invalid name extraction\n   103→- Added check to reject names starting/ending with non-alphabetic characters\n   104→- Result: Pipeline no longer fails on \"--yes\" from spaCy mis-tagging\n   105→\n   106→### Attempt 3 (2026-01-18): Added food/beverage filter\n   107→- Added `FOOD_BEVERAGE_NAMES` set with 24 common food/drink terms\n   108→- Pre-filter check before LLM validation\n   109→- Result: Score improved 6.10 → 7.70 (+1.60 points)\n   110→\n   111→### Attempt 4 (2026-01-18): Narrator-aware profiling\n   112→- Root cause: Passage gatherer searches for character names; first-person narrators use \"I\" not their name\n   113→- Modified: src/pipeline/character_profiling/passage_gatherer.py:gather_passages()\n   114→  - Added _find_narrator_passages() method at line 98\n   115→  - For is_narrator=true characters, searches for \"I\", \"my\", \"me\" pronouns instead of names\n   116→  - Samples ~50 passages evenly distributed across text\n   117→- Modified: src/pipeline/character_profiling/pipeline.py:89-118\n   118→  - Added defensive check to ensure narrator flag is set after identification\n   119→  - Logs warning if narrator name doesn't match any character\n   120→- Modified: src/pipeline/character_profiling/converter.py:_estimate_mention_count()\n   121→  - Boosts mention_count to minimum 100 for first-person narrators\n   122→  - Reflects narrative presence vs explicit name mentions\n   123→- Smoke test: Unit tests pass (444 passed, 11 skipped)\n   124→- Full pipeline test: Unable to complete due to Ollama server issues (model loading errors)\n   125→\n   126→## Output Files (Attempt 3)\n   127→- HTML: output/cask_of_amontillado/report.html\n   128→- JSON: output/cask_of_amontillado/analysis.json\n   129→\n   130→## Next Action\n   131→**Phase:** awaiting_analysis\n   132→\n   133→Run PROMPT_fix.md to address Issue #1 (Montresor missing profile).\n   134→\n   135→**Recommended Fix Approach:**\n   136→The narrator profile problem requires a conceptual change:\n   137→1. When the plot_summary identifies a first-person narrator (e.g., \"Montresor, the story's first-person narrator\")\n   138→2. Extract that character name\n   139→3. Build their profile from first-person statements (\"I vowed revenge\", \"I led him deeper\", etc.)\n   140→4. Also set `is_narrator: true` for that character\n   141→\n   142→This is a cross-component fix involving:\n   143→- `src/agents/summary_agent.py` (narrator identification)\n   144→- `src/pipeline/character_extraction/` (profile building)\n   145→- Character metadata sync\n   146→\n   147→**Alternative Quick Fix:**\n   148→If the narrator-aware profile building is too complex, focus on just:\n   149→- Lowering the mention count threshold to include Luchresi (6 mentions)\n   150→- Fixing the `is_narrator` flag sync\n   151→\n   152→This simpler fix might get us the 0.30 points needed.\n   153→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f700d47e-f086-4db4-997e-7b427eb3c6e7","uuid":"0e0f5e0d-751a-44af-9831-ee933fb7d61f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/EVALUATION_STATE.md","content":"## Fix History\n\n### Attempt 1 (2026-01-18): Fixed validator heuristic\n- Removed overly aggressive auto-acceptance of high-mention-count names\n- Enhanced validation system prompt to reject objects/food/drink\n- Result: Amontillado no longer extracted, narrator correctly identified in plot_summary\n\n### Attempt 2 (2026-01-18): Fixed NER invalid name extraction\n- Added check to reject names starting/ending with non-alphabetic characters\n- Result: Pipeline no longer fails on \"--yes\" from spaCy mis-tagging\n\n### Attempt 3 (2026-01-18): Added food/beverage filter\n- Added `FOOD_BEVERAGE_NAMES` set with 24 common food/drink terms\n- Pre-filter check before LLM validation\n- Result: Score improved 6.10 → 7.70 (+1.60 points)\n\n### Attempt 4 (2026-01-18): Narrator-aware profiling\n- Root cause: Passage gatherer searches for character names; first-person narrators use \"I\" not their name\n- Modified: src/pipeline/character_profiling/passage_gatherer.py:gather_passages()\n  - Added _find_narrator_passages() method at line 98\n  - For is_narrator=true characters, searches for \"I\", \"my\", \"me\" pronouns instead of names\n  - Samples ~50 passages evenly distributed across text\n- Modified: src/pipeline/character_profiling/pipeline.py:89-118\n  - Added defensive check to ensure narrator flag is set after identification\n  - Logs warning if narrator name doesn't match any character\n- Modified: src/pipeline/character_profiling/converter.py:_estimate_mention_count()\n  - Boosts mention_count to minimum 100 for first-person narrators\n  - Reflects narrative presence vs explicit name mentions\n- Smoke test: Unit tests pass (444 passed, 11 skipped)\n- Full pipeline test: Unable to complete due to Ollama server issues (model loading errors)\n\n## Output Files (Attempt 3)\n- HTML: output/cask_of_amontillado/report.html\n- JSON: output/cask_of_amontillado/analysis.json\n\n## Next Action\n**Phase:** awaiting_analysis\n\nRun PROMPT_fix.md to address Issue #1 (Montresor missing profile).\n\n**Recommended Fix Approach:**\nThe narrator profile problem requires a conceptual change:\n1. When the plot_summary identifies a first-person narrator (e.g., \"Montresor, the story's first-person narrator\")\n2. Extract that character name\n3. Build their profile from first-person statements (\"I vowed revenge\", \"I led him deeper\", etc.)\n4. Also set `is_narrator: true` for that character\n\nThis is a cross-component fix involving:\n- `src/agents/summary_agent.py` (narrator identification)\n- `src/pipeline/character_extraction/` (profile building)\n- Character metadata sync\n\n**Alternative Quick Fix:**\nIf the narrator-aware profile building is too complex, focus on just:\n- Lowering the mention count threshold to include Luchresi (6 mentions)\n- Fixing the `is_narrator` flag sync\n\nThis simpler fix might get us the 0.30 points needed.\n","numLines":59,"startLine":95,"totalLines":153}}}
